# Claude API Cost Analysis — Automated Trading Bot

## How Your Bot Uses the API

Your bot makes **2 API calls per cycle**, running every **5 minutes** (288 cycles/day):

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A["⏰ Every 5 min"] --> B["1️⃣ Orchestrator Agent"]
    B -->|analyze=true ~50%| C["2️⃣ Trend Agent"]
    B -->|analyze=false ~50%| D["Sleep 60s"]
    C --> E["Risk Manager ❌ No API"]
    E --> F["Executor ❌ No API"]
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Only the **Orchestrator** and **Trend Agent** call Claude. Risk manager, executor, data feed, indicators — all run locally with **zero API cost**.

---

## Token Usage Per Call

| Component | System Prompt | User Prompt (data) | Output | Total Input | Total Output |
|-----------|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|
| **Orchestrator** | ~330 tokens | ~350 tokens | ~70 tokens | **680 tokens** | **70 tokens** |
| **Trend Agent** | ~400 tokens | ~300 tokens | ~120 tokens | **700 tokens** | **120 tokens** |
| **Backtest Analysis** (occasional) | ~100 tokens | ~1,000 tokens | ~1,500 tokens | **1,100 tokens** | **1,500 tokens** |

